<main id="main" class="container">
  <h1>About curve-lab</h1>
  <p>A workshop for curves that can be built exactly, and for the ornaments that
    follow from them. A curve is written as a pair of polynomials with
    whole-number coefficients, so its grid, bend, symmetry and self-crossings
    are computed in exact fractions rather than floats.</p>
  <p>The older layer is the Euler curve — curvature rising in proportion to arc
    length — built as a chain and written as plain SVG that Inkscape opens as
    ordinary nodes. The newer layer is the exact integer curve, and the book
    plates are built from it.</p>

  <h2>Read more</h2>
  <ul>
    {links.map((link) => (
      <li><a href={link.href}>{link.label}</a> — {link.note}</li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2>Run it</h2>
  <p>The lab pages are generated into <code>workbench/</code> and served by
    <code>scripts/serve.py</code> on port 8003. This app is the Astro layer on
    port 4321, and the prose book is the same app, at <code>/docs</code>.</p>
</main>
</body></html>
